@hthieblot One day, I pissed off Dean Hachamovitch, who ran Internet Explorer at Microsoft, because I was like, "Why can't we move faster? Why can't we be more open? Why can't we do this? Why can't we do that?" 

He pulled me into his office—quite nicely, I might add—and explained to me all the constituencies that he has to serve and all the meetings he has to attend. Some people want the opposite of what another team wants, so it's not just your team against the other internal teams; it could be two internal teams against you. 

That is why a startup can outrun a big company: they don't need to care about all the constituencies, because they have none yet.

@Financewisdom01 The guy who started Waze told me everyone is a bag of human patterns. 

The algorithms can do things we can’t.

Like what if all the teslas in a parking lot started working together to see the grandmas passing behind in wheelchairs that are hard to see in mirrors.

